{"id": "p1_00251", "question": "Bert fills out the daily crossword puzzle in the newspaper every day. He uses up a pencil to fill out the puzzles every two weeks. On average, it takes him 1050 words to use up a pencil. How many words are in each crossword puzzle on average?", "trace": "It takes Bert one pencil for every two weeks of filling out crosswords.\nIn two weeks, there are 14 days. Assuming he does a crossword every single day as stated (\"every day\"), he completes 14 puzzles per pencil.\nWe know that one pencil lasts for 1050 words.\nTo find the average number of words per puzzle, we divide the total word count by the number of puzzles completed with that pencil.\nCalculation: $1050 \\div 14$.\nStep-by-step division:\n$1050 / 14$:\nBoth numbers are divisible by 7.\n$1050 / 7 = 150$\n$14 / 7 = 2$\nNow, calculate $150 / 2$.\n$150 / 2 = 75$.\n\nAlternatively:\n$14 \\times 70 = 980$\n$1050 - 980 = 70$\n$14 \\times 5 = 70$\n$70 + 5 = 75$.\n\nSo, on average, there are 75 words in each crossword puzzle.\n#### 75", "gold_solution": "At 7 days a week, it takes Bert 2 * 7 = <<2*7=14>>14 days of daily crossword puzzles to use up a pencil.\nSince Bert does one puzzle a day, each crossword puzzle has 1050 / 14 = <<1050/14=75>>75 words.\n#### 75", "gold_answer": 75.0, "label": "GOOD", "diagnosis": null, "diagnosis_reason": null, "diagnosis_confidence": null, "signals": {"E": 1.0, "V": 1.0, "R": 1.0, "A": 0.5, "G": 1.0, "coherent": true, "correct": true, "final_answer": 75.0, "misses": 0, "bad_eqs": 0, "n_steps": 18, "n_checkpoints": 2, "n_equations": 5, "r_variant": "dup_fraction", "E_struct": 0.0, "A_struct": 0.0, "E_eff": 1.0, "n_comp_steps": 5, "comp_coverage": 2.5, "n_symbolic": 0, "n_unresolved": 2, "truncated": false}, "complexity": 2, "stored_at": 1790515466.937793, "retried": false, "embedding": [0.04737861454486847, -0.032982487231492996, 0.07576616108417511, -0.018487704917788506, -0.1007816269993782, 0.05122630298137665, 0.059802908450365067, 0.03902889043092