{"id": "p1_00262", "question": "The seats of a bus are arranged in 23 rows of 4 seats. At the start, 16 people climb. At the first stop, 15 people board the bus and 3 get off. At the second stop, 17 people get on the bus and 10 get off. How many empty seats are there after the second stop?", "trace": "First, calculate the total capacity of the bus.\nTotal seats = 23 rows $\\times$ 4 seats/row = 92 seats.\n\nNext, track the number of passengers throughout the trip.\nStart: 16 people on the bus.\nStop 1: 15 people board (+15) and 3 get off (-3).\nChange at Stop 1 = $15 - 3 = 12$.\nPassengers after Stop 1 = $16 + 12 = 28$.\n\nStop 2: 17 people get on (+17) and 10 get off (-10).\nChange at Stop 2 = $17 - 10 = 7$.\nPassengers after Stop 2 = $28 + 7 = 35$.\n\nFinally, calculate the number of empty seats.\nEmpty seats = Total seats - Current passengers.\nEmpty seats = $92 - 35$.\n$92 - 35 = 57$.\n\nThere are 57 empty seats.\n#### 57", "gold_solution": "There are 23 * 4 = <<23*4=92>>92 seats on this bus.\nAfter the first stop, there are 16+15 - 3 = <<16+15-3=28>>28 people on the bus.\nAfter the 2nd stop, there are 28+17 - 10 = <<28+17-10=35>>35 people on the bus.\nSo there are 92 - 35 = <<92-35=57>>57 empty seats on the bus after the 2nd stop.\n#### 57", "gold_answer": 57.0, "label": "GOOD", "diagnosis": null, "diagnosis_reason": null, "diagnosis_confidence": null, "signals": {"E": 1.0, "V": 1.0, "R": 1.0, "A": 0.75, "G": 1.0, "coherent": true, "correct": true, "final_answer": 57.0, "misses": 0, "bad_eqs": 0, "n_steps": 15, "n_checkpoints": 4, "n_equations": 5, "r_variant": "dup_fraction", "E_struct": 0.25, "A_struct": 0.25, "E_eff": 1.0, "n_comp_steps": 5, "comp_coverage": 1.25, "n_symbolic": 0, "n_unresolved": 3, "truncated": false}, "complexity": 4, "stored_at": 1790515835.6321008, "retried": false, "embedding": [0.0758209228515625, 0.02835383638739586, 0.04353441670536995, -0.055981267243623734, -0.02595638483762741, 0.07247798144817352, 0.036468952894210815, 0.02814719